   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- `fieldnotes/cli.py:22` prints `note['created']` as it is stored, with no reformatting.\n- `fieldnotes/store.py:25` sets that value with `moment.isoformat()`. It comes out like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`, which is ISO-8601 with a UTC offset.\n- I found no `strftime`, `toLocale`, or other locale-style formatting anywhere in the code. The only other output that could carry a date is the `added:` line in `cli.py:18`, and it prints just the text.\n\nNothing needs changing. The risk is that `list` shows whatever string is in the store, so a note saved by another tool or an older version in a different format would be printed as is. If you want a guarantee, `list` could parse and re-emit the value with `datetime.fromisoformat(...).isoformat()`. I haven't made that change.",
   "suspended": false
  },
