   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`. It prints one `DATE: TEXT` line per note, for example `2026-01-02: first`. The project checks pass: both tests ran and the line-length rule found nothing.\n\n- **Date format:** I took `DATE` to mean the date part of the stored timestamp (`YYYY-MM-DD`). If you'd rather have the full ISO timestamp, change `created[:10]` to `created` in `fieldnotes/cli.py`.\n- **Usage message:** I moved the usage string into one `USAGE` constant that now lists `export`. The two places that printed it use the constant.\n- **Test:** the new test is in `tests/test_cli.py`. It adds two notes and checks the exported lines.\n- **Checks:** `tools/check.py` requires `NOTES_HOME` to be set, so I ran it with a temporary directory. You'll need to set it too when you run the checks.",
